{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDT9qJ1tAy6KeUQaZG5T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LKeKCPv6GH2txnQFYx8s8h","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"A=\"/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python ../skill/scripts/answer.py brace-findings.json\"\n$A check A05.1 --met no --evidence app/identity.py:63 --quote 'def compute_agent_type_id(manifest: dict) -> str:' --note \"Both IDs are written on every audit row (audit.py:86-88), but the type ID is only a hash of manifest content. Nothing stores manifests keyed by that ID (no registry, table or file), and startup only logs it (startup.py:45). No pod name or label carries the instance ID, so it does not resolve to a live pod.\" \n$A check A05.2 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:4 --quote 'owner: team-procurement-platform' --note \"Ownership is a single team name. No CODEOWNERS, catalog-info or .brace/deployment.yaml exists. Nothing names a current operator or on-call rotation, and the two agent types (procurement, extractor) have no per-type mapping. operational_owner defaults to the same team string (settings.py:86).\"\n$A check A05.3 --met no --evidence app/killswitch.py:19 --quote \"AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = \\$1)\" --note \"The only stop control is a control_flags row scoped to the whole fleet or one tenant. There is no per-instance or per-agent-type scope. assert_running is called only at run start (loop.py:127), so it does not reach a running instance. No token-revocation or scale-to-zero control is in the repo.\"\n$A check A06.1 --met no --evidence app/identity.py:50 --quote 'def child(self, role: str) -> \"RunIdentity\":' --note \"child() issues a new instance ID (identity.py:53) but copies the parent's agent_type_id through dataclasses.replace. The extractor uses a different model and prompt yet shares the parent's type ID. It is the only spawn path (extractor.py:44).\"\n$A check A06.3 --met no --evidence deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:67 --quote 'value: \"false\"' --note \"OTEL_INSTRUMENTATION_GENAI_CAPTURE_MESSAGE_CONTENT is explicitly false. The subagent_started record holds only role, doc_id, tools and a span id labelled parent_prompt_ref (extractor.py:55-60), not the prompt text or a hash. The task string built at extractor.py:46 is not recorded.\"\n$A check A06.4 --met unknown --evidence app/audit.py:116 --quote 'json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),' --note \"No parent-to-child prompt text is captured (A06.3), so there is no prompt store to check. audit_events payloads pass through redact_value, but the migration grants audit_events SELECT to procurement_ops (001_init.sql:132), not a named audit role. No IAM or ACL for a prompt store exists in this repo.\"\n$A check A07.2 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:37 --quote 'models:' --note \"Model IDs are pinned snapshots (manifest.yaml:42,54) and match the deployment env (deployment.yaml:41,43). But the model records hold no prompt reference or configuration. max_tokens 4096 (extractor.py:71, loop.py:147) and MAX_TURNS (extractor.py:26) are hard-coded inline and absent from the inventory.\"\n$A check A07.4 --met no --evidence app/extractor.py:80 --quote '\"served_model\": response.model,' --note \"served_model is logged but never compared with the pinned model ID, in extractor.py:80 or loop.py:158. A swapped or drifted model does not fail anything. Parse errors do fail closed (extractor.py:105-106). No judge or guardrail model exists.\"\n$A check C01.1 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:34 --quote 'network_policy: deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml' --note \"network_policy and image_policy are bare paths with no digest or version (manifest.yaml:34-35). Permission scopes are not a manifest category. They exist only inside policy.yaml (policy.yaml:18-29). No entries for MCP protocol/extension version, OIDC issuer/audience binding, or cache/task isolation settings. The header says CI regenerates the manifest (manifest.yaml:1-2), but ci.yaml only checks hashes.\"\n$A check C01.4 --met no --evidence release/manifest.yaml:34 --quote 'network_policy: deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml' --note \"Only the models and mcp_servers.erp carry owners. image, harness, prompts, config, memory and identity have none. network_policy and image_policy have no digest or commit though the files are in the repo. The ERP MCP endpoint is a service URL with no version pin.\"\n$A check C02.1 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yaml:5 --quote 'push:' --note \"No CODEOWNERS file exists anywhere in the repo, so manifest, prompts, tools.yaml and policy.yaml have no review owner. CI runs on push to main with no review condition. Branch protection lives in the hosting service and is not visible. Git tracking cannot be checked: the workspace has no .git. Files are baked into the image, not loaded from a remote URL (Dockerfile:17-19).\"\n$A check C02.2 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yaml:40 --quote \"if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\" --note \"The release job has no environment: key, so no protected environment gates it. It runs on any push to main. No CODEOWNERS or IAM config names who can change production config.\"\n$A check C02.3 --met unknown --evidence README.md:55 --quote '## Operating' --note \"Searched the whole repo for emergency, break-glass, on-call, runbook. The README Operating section covers only halt (control_flags) and release. No emergency config-change path, owner, end date or follow-up review is in the repo. The procedure may live in an outside runbook (killswitch.py:4 refers to a platform runbook).\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1738,"cache_read_input_tokens":67463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1738},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"sta