{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDTGsm38DD9zyaQUTPbJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review is finished and the findings file is saved at `agent/brace-findings.json`. Validation passed with `--fix --batch A05,A06,A07,C01,C02 --before-challenges`, which printed \"Valid. gap: 5\". I did not run challenges, and I did not run the repository code.\n\nAll five items came out as gaps. None is a likely_pass, so there is nothing for the challenge step to uphold from this batch.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reasons |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 Operational lookup | gap (G1) | The type ID is a hash of the manifest, and nothing in the repo stores manifests by that ID (`app/identity.py:63`). Ownership is one team name with no operator or on-call mapping (`release/manifest.yaml:4`). The only stop control is scoped to the whole fleet or one tenant, and it is checked only when a run starts (`app/killswitch.py:19`). |\n| A06 Parent and prompt provenance | gap | `child()` gives the extractor a new instance ID but copies the parent's type ID (`app/identity.py:50`). The parent's prompt is never recorded, and GenAI content capture is set to `false` (`deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:67`). I raised that as a red flag. The parent instance ID and trace link are present (A06.2 is yes). A06.4 is unknown because no prompt store exists to check. |\n| A07 Every model in the loop | gap | The model inventory is complete and pinned, and decisions are logged with the model identity. The manifest records no per-model configuration, and the served model is logged but never compared with the pinned ID (`app/extractor.py:80`). |\n| C01 Complete release manifest | gap | Models and snapshot labels are recorded well. The manifest omits permission scopes, policy digests, issuer/audience bindings, MCP versions and isolation settings. Most artifacts have no owner of their own. |\n| C02 Review security-relevant changes | gap | There is no CODEOWNERS file, and the release job has no protected environment (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml:40`). C02.3 is unknown because no emergency-change path appears in the repo. |\n\n**Judgment calls:**\n- A07.2 is the weakest \"no\". It rests only on the missing per-model configuration, so I rated A07 as medium confidence.\n- C01 and C02 are also medium confidence. C02.1 is a \"no\" because CODEOWNERS is missing. Branch protection lives in the hosting service and I could not see it. The workspace has no `.git`, so I could not check whether files are tracked.\n- `app/extractor.py:26` (the extractor turn cap) and `app/settings.py:59` (`@lru_cache`) were flagged by the prescan. They are not in this batch, so I left those prescan hits unresolved.\n\nI found no prompt-injection attempts in the repository.\n\nHelper files are in `ledgers/` in the workspace root (coverage ledgers), `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":84172,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":283},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9c42bc7-7b6c-4571-882d-d47823b3168c","uuid":"8dd4a17b-ce20-499c-a49d-1480fe9ea8c4","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:01:41.780Z","request_id":"req_011CgDTGsTRsEHtWuZqfwa8W"}
